# NTFS Permissions

- NTFS = New Technology File System
- Permissions control access to files/folders

## Types of Permissions

- Full Control
- Modify
- Read & Execute
- List Folder Contents
- Read
- Write

# Viewing Permissions

- Right-click file/folder
- Open Properties
- Go to Security tab
- View users and permissions

# Alternate Data Streams (ADS)

- Feature of NTFS
- Allows multiple data streams in one file
- Used to hide/store extra data
- Can be viewed using PowerShell
- Sometimes abused by malware

# Windows Folder & System32

- Windows folder usually located at:
  - C:\Windows
- System variable:
  - %windir%
- System32 contains important OS files
- Deleting System32 files can damage Windows

# User Accounts

## Types of Accounts

- Administrator
- Standard User

## Administrator

- Can change system settings
- Can add/remove users
- Can install programs

## Standard User

- Limited permissions
- Cannot make system-level changes

# User Profiles

- Stored in:
  - C:\Users
- Common folders:
  - Desktop
  - Documents
  - Downloads
  - Music
  - Pictures

# Local Users and Groups

- Open Run dialog
- Type:
  - lusrmgr.msc
- Shows:
  - Users
  - Groups
- Users inherit group permissions

# User Account Control (UAC)

- UAC = User Account Control
- Prevents unauthorized system changes
- Prompts for admin permission before installing/changing system files
- Shield icon indicates admin privileges required

# Settings vs Control Panel

## Settings

- Modern Windows configuration tool
- Easier and touch-friendly

## Control Panel

- Traditional management tool
- Used for advanced settings

# Programs and Features

- Located in Control Panel
- Used to:
  - View installed programs
  - Uninstall software
  - Repair applications
